          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ぼうし (boushi) is Sino-Japanese (kango): two Chinese characters read with their on'yomi, readings borrowed from Chinese. They are bō, \"hat\" (Middle Chinese mawH) and shi, \"child; a noun ending\" (tsiX) (Unihan, KANJIDIC2; Middle Chinese in Baxter's transcription)."
            }
          ]
        },
